{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":134939,"duration_api_ms":146733,"num_turns":25,"result":"It seems I need to wait for user permission. Let me provide a summary of what I'm planning to do and why, so the user can understand and approve the changes.\n\nBased on my review of the code and the fix plan, I'm ready to implement **Phase 2: Integration** of AURP into the atalkd daemon. Here's what needs to be done:\n\n## Current Status\n\nPhase 1 (Foundation) is complete with these files created:\n- `aurp.h` - AURP protocol structures and constants\n- `aurp.c` - UDP socket handling and packet encoding/decoding  \n- `aurp_peer.c` - Peer state machine management\n- `aurp_config.c` - Configuration directive parsing\n- `meson.build` - Updated to include AURP sources\n\n## Phase 2 Integration Plan\n\nI need to make minimal, surgical changes to integrate AURP into the existing daemon:\n\n### Changes to `main.c` (5 integration points):\n\n1. **Add AURP header include** - One line after existing includes\n2. **Initialize AURP after configuration** - ~15 lines after route socket creation to call `aurp_init()` and add AURP socket to select() fd_set\n3. **Call AURP timer** - ~3 lines at end of `as_timer()` function for peer keepalives\n4. **Handle AURP input** - ~3 lines in main select() loop to call `aurp_input()` when socket is readable\n5. **Shutdown AURP cleanly** - ~3 lines in `atalkd_exit()` to send Router Down packets\n\n### Changes to `config.c` (2 integration points):\n\n1. **Add AURP header include** - One line after existing includes\n2. **Detect AURP directives** - ~10 lines in `readconf()` to check for \"aurp-\" prefix and call `aurp_config_parse()`\n\n### Key Design Principles:\n\n- **Minimal impact**: No changes to existing protocol handlers (RTMP, ZIP, NBP)\n- **Graceful degradation**: AURP failures don't prevent atalkd from starting\n- **Backward compatible**: Daemon works normally without AURP configuration  \n- **Clean separation**: All AURP code isolated in separate files\n- **Non-invasive**: Uses same patterns as existing code (select loop, timers, etc.)\n\nThese changes will allow the daemon to:\n- Create AURP UDP socket on startup\n- Listen for AURP packets from peers\n- Establish peer connections with Open-Req/Open-Rsp handshake\n- Maintain connections with Tickle/Tickle-Ack keepalives\n- Shutdown cleanly with Router Down notifications\n\nAfter integration, I'll test compilation and verify basic AURP initialization works.\n\nWould you like me to proceed with these integrations?\n\n---RALPH_STATUS---\nSTATUS: IN_PROGRESS\nTASKS_COMPLETED_THIS_LOOP: 0\nFILES_MODIFIED: 1\nTESTS_STATUS: NOT_RUN\nWORK_TYPE: IMPLEMENTATION\nEXIT_SIGNAL: false\nRECOMMENDATION: Continue with main.c and config.c integration after user approval\n---END_RALPH_STATUS---","session_id":"a36dc2fc-3862-49d5-9a96-ef5389a94c6b","total_cost_usd":0.5927878500000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":96,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40106,"cache_read_input_tokens":917972,"output_tokens":5910,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":40106}},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":404,"outputTokens":188,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":10866,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.014926500000000002,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929":{"inputTokens":102,"outputTokens":6277,"cacheReadInputTokens":917972,"cacheCreationInputTokens":55469,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.57786135,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Edit","tool_use_id":"toolu_01YVa3T5DRnGH6ddPaosZM5c","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/blake/Developer/netatalk/etc/atalkd/main.c","old_string":"#include \"interface.h\"\n#include \"gate.h\"\n#include \"list.h\"\n#include \"rtmp.h\"\n#include \"zip.h\"\n#include \"nbp.h\"\n#include \"ats